# Commercial S10.2A — S9 timer recovery evidence

Date: 2026-09-03
Decision: AUTOMATED_WMS_SFW_GROWTH = GO

## Scope and boundaries

This evidence covers the backup-first restoration of the existing public-SFW
S9 audience, nurture and health schedules. No Adult media, identity document,
real AVS, payment, external Adult publishing, creator activation, controlled
beta or production capability was opened. No token, message, media or personal
data was captured in this evidence.

## Provenance

- Canonical application: `4c1d4d8eb72155c3eb28bf228096eb3cdfd18d1e`
  (tree `290b28bb2560d77e4282431785fa34c16f41a927`).
- Deployed application release intentionally unchanged:
  `deeb38c30427066989eb85e1c115d2aeccf140cf`
  (tree `3619e7dc557b49c632efa713bb0bc4214fd83fca`).
- Operational Control accepted before this evidence-only integration:
  `23257227b2c70ef1639d051393e67b03903d78e8`
  (tree `07039ddb8635522e36b01f18f5dc2dabbd829aa6`).
- Operational Control CI: run `33770768136`, success.
- Full local Control suite: 378/378 green.
- Final Control and application checkouts were clean.

## Before

The audience, nurture and S9 health timers were active and enabled but had no
future elapse. They used stale `OnUnitActiveSec` anchors whose backing service
activation timestamps no longer provided a live schedule.

## Backup and rollback

- Pre-final-sync Control bundle:
  `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s9-timer-liveness/20260903T150943Z-pre-control-sync-final`
- Pre-final-repair systemd/script surface:
  `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s9-timer-liveness/20260903T150946Z-pre-repair`
- Both SHA-256 indexes verified.
- The Control bundle passed `git bundle verify`.
- The versioned repair retained automatic file restoration, timer stop and
  Control rollback on failure. No final rollback was invoked.

## Installed correction

- Audience: persistent calendar anchor every 15 minutes at minute 00/15/30/45.
- Nurture: persistent calendar anchor every 15 minutes at minute 03/18/33/48.
- S9 health: persistent calendar anchor every five minutes at minute 04/09/14/etc.
- Stale S9 audience and S9 health service definitions were refreshed from SSOT.
- S9 health and S10 health envelopes reject timers without a future elapse.
- Each health envelope narrowly tolerates only its own actively running timer,
  because systemd calculates the next `OnUnitActiveSec` elapse after the
  service completes. Waiting timers without a future elapse remain RED.
- Installed S10 health SHA-256 matched Control SSOT:
  `d9e15f44c6d0708d7e692cf13ce44699b3c0477815609fe50893d88b3c3f4f72`.

